  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bolivia Research UMSS 2021-2027 - NEW Swedish Universities ISP UMSS 2021-2027</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bolivia forskning UMSS 2021-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">General objective:

Contribute to develop the region, the country, and universal knowledge by creating high quality and impactful knowledge to be transferred to and used by the social/productive sector

Specific strategic objectives:

Research training: Implement programmes and projects in institutional, regional, and national interest areas, with results acknowledged and used by the scientific community and in the socio-productive environment, and closely linked to local postgraduate programmes in science within sector and national development plans.

Research-support component: Create a favourable environment for SICTI to develop programmes to train researchers, and in research and innovation activities, with a proper and efficient management system that includes environmental management, quality assurance, and a gender/non-discrimination perspective.

Specific objectives:

1. Increase the critical mass of MSc and PhD researchers by means of local postgraduate programmes in science of the sandwich modality

2. Increase R&amp;D&amp;I projects under many support modalities that further knowledge in general and/or respond to regional and national issues

3. Implement support modalities driving and privileging research careers at UMSS

4. Promote an institutional university-socio productive environment relation to encourage innovation at UMSS

5. Institute quality assurance criteria to run postgraduate courses in science and their corresponding research activities

6. Create a favourable environment to develop research and innovation activities with a university social responsibility approach</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det offentliga universitetet &quot;Universidad Mayor de San Sim&#xf3;n&quot; (UMSS) i Cochabamba, Bolivia, har ans&#xf6;kt hos Sida om finansiering f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra programmet &quot;St&#xe4;rka institutionell forskningskapacitet i Universidad Mayor de San Sim&#xf3;n 2021-2025&quot;.

Insatsen syftar till att utveckla vetenskap och forskning i Bolivia s&#xe4;rskilt i Cochabambaregionen, genom produktion av h&#xf6;gkvalitativ och inflytelserik vetenskap som ska &#xf6;verf&#xf6;ras till och anv&#xe4;ndas av sociala sektorer och n&#xe4;ringslivet genom:
1.) forskarutbildning f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka antalet forskare med doktorsexamen och st&#xe4;rka forskningskapaciteten inom omr&#xe5;den som &#xe4;r relevanta f&#xf6;r utveckling; 
2) utveckling av en milj&#xf6; vid UMSS som gynnar vetenskap, teknik och innovation. 
3) utveckling av en universitetsmilj&#xf6; som fr&#xe4;mjar j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och milj&#xf6;arbete i universitetet sj&#xe4;lvt

Insatsens totala budget &#xe4;r ca 283,3 miljoner SEK av vilka ca 151 miljoner SEK &#xe4;r UMSS eget bidrag. Budgeten inkluderar Sidas bidrag till insatsen f&#xf6;r 132,3 miljoner SEK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The public university &quot;Universidad Mayor de San Sim&#xf3;n&quot; (UMSS) in Cochabamba, Bolivia, has applied to Sida for funding to carry out the program &quot;Strengthening institutional research capacities in Universidad Mayor de San Sim&#xf3;n 2021-2025&quot;.

The intervention aims &quot;to develop science and research in Bolivia, especially in the Cochabamba region, through the production of high-quality and impact-full science to be transferred to and used by the social sectors and the business community by: 1) research training to increase the number of researchers with PhD graduation and strengthen research capacity in areas relevant to scientific and social development; 
2) development of an environment at UMSS that favors science, technology and innovation.
3) development of a university environment that promotes gender equality and environmental work in the university itself.
The intervention&apos;s total budget is approximately 283,3 million SEK, out of which UMSS&apos; own funding is approximately 151 million SEK. The budget includes Sida&#xb4;s grants for 132,3 million SEK.</narrative>
  </description>
